{"text":"Builder: repair the burned jsonataddl v0.1.0 release contract and prepare the first usable v0.1.1 module release.","body":{"conditions":"Work from exact current main db5446775c7382ccf8095ab17581f61411f276fa in a new request/jsonataddl-v011-recovery branch and worktree. Never move or delete the existing jsonataddl/v0.1.0 tag. In jsonataddl/go.mod retract v0.1.0 with a plain-English reason naming the immutable checksum collision; change the root go.mod requirement behind its local replace to v0.1.1; update current release documentation and jsonataddl/README.md to advertise v0.1.1 and clearly warn that v0.1.0 is permanently unusable. Do not rewrite the historical architecture note merely to change its historical example. Add a pre-tag release check that refuses a module version already recorded by proxy.golang.org or sum.golang.org, distinguishes verified absence from network or malformed-response failure, has bounded network behavior, and is covered by deterministic injected/local fixtures rather than live-network CI tests. Document that this check must run before pushing a version tag. Preserve the existing post-push tag workflow. Configure a GitHub ruleset protecting jsonataddl/v* from deletion and non-fast-forward updates, and record the ruleset evidence without treating it as source review. Run focused tests, full tests, race, vet, nested-module verification, and clean-checkout/module-boundary checks. Publish exact-path artifacts on an exact source head and obtain independent Architecture, Security, and Simplification review. Merge only the ratified approved exact head to main, push, require main CI green, and clean the feature branch/worktree without rm -f or rm -rf. Do not create or publish v0.1.1 in this source-repair task; Hugh will file that as a separate no-source task after the landed repair is verified.","stale_bases":"git:sha1:da732b0bdaad4426ed4ad666b892d8a7c68f625f#git:sha1:69223dcdb954f4f3ebb4a855adab26d3084974d6, git:sha1:da732b0bdaad4426ed4a